From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:14:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] S5: devicebasedauth.org section and link callback in the
 workspace

The Account page gains a devicebasedauth.org section: link status (or a
superseded link), Link/Unlink, the DBA credentials seen on the account with
their monthly caps and expiry, and instructions for device-bound keys
(`dba enroll --aud cronly.org --action cronly:run`, `dba curl`, `dba token`)
and the browser SDK (`import { DBA } from
'https://devicebasedauth.org/sdk/dba.js'`). All dynamic text is escaped.

/auth/dba/callback serves the workspace, which moves code/state out of the
address bar and history immediately (sessionStorage) and posts them to
/api/dba/link/finish once signed in, so a sign-in in between still works.
A Playwright test covers the callback, URL cleanup and escaping.

